    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 10 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Be the first player to run out of all your cards. You win when you play your last card(s) and are not successfully challenged, or when you have no cards left and it is your turn to lead a new round.',
      "Turn-flow example: 1. The lead player plays 1-3 cards face-down and declares a rank (e.g., 'Three Kings').\n2. The next player MUST play the same rank. They can tell the truth or lie.\n3. This continues until a player is challenged or everyone passes (starting a new rank).",
      "Scoring example: First player to get rid of all their cards and survive any challenge on their final play wins the deal. For multi-deal play, a common convention is one penalty point per card remaining in each loser's hand; lowest total wins. First player to get rid of all their cards wins..",
